Subject: [PATCH] rapier - 1.8 combat: sprint/KB-enchant extra knockback via
 1.8.9 addVelocity semantics

1.8.9 applied the sprint / Knockback-enchant bonus as a pure addVelocity
on top of the base knockback: (-sin(yaw) * i * 0.5, +0.1, cos(yaw) * i * 0.5).
modern routes it through LivingEntity.knockback() which halves the
target current motion AGAIN (the base hit already halved it) and
re-applies a capped vertical kick. measured on a standing ground target,
a sprint hit lands at ~0.7 horizontal / 0.40 vertical instead of the
authentic ~0.9 / 0.46 -- weaker sends and no bounce above the cap.

replaced with Entity.push(), which has exact addVelocity semantics and
fires the Paper EntityPushedByEntityAttackEvent for plugin compat.
hurtMarked=true delivers the motion to the victim client through the
existing CraftBukkit velocity block (which also restores the pre-hit
server motion, same as 1.8 d0/d1/d2 restore). knockback-scale from
rapier.properties applies to the extra so the tuning knob keeps
covering the full hit.

strength magnitudes were already equivalent (getKnockback returns
ench/2 and sprint adds 0.5, matching 1.8 i*0.5) -- only the
application semantics changed.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/player/Player.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/player/Player.java
index 4db2fa629a3cd988ac5d9d01ecfee885d2d9a355..04a0e33757da953f42fe0cae8ed6b5ebc1e45776 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/player/Player.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/player/Player.java
@@ -1202,14 +1202,25 @@ public abstract class Player extends Avatar implements ContainerUser {
     @Override
     public void causeExtraKnockback(Entity target, float strength, Vec3 currentMovement) {
         if (strength > 0.0F) {
-            if (target instanceof LivingEntity livingEntity) {
-                livingEntity.knockback(strength, Mth.sin(this.getYRot() * (float) (Math.PI / 180.0)), -Mth.cos(this.getYRot() * (float) (Math.PI / 180.0)), this, io.papermc.paper.event.entity.EntityKnockbackEvent.Cause.ENTITY_ATTACK); // Paper - knockback events
-            } else {
-                target.push(
-                    -Mth.sin(this.getYRot() * (float) (Math.PI / 180.0)) * strength, 0.1, Mth.cos(this.getYRot() * (float) (Math.PI / 180.0)) * strength
-                    , this // Paper - Add EntityKnockbackByEntityEvent and EntityPushedByEntityAttackEvent
-                );
-            }
+            // rapier start - 1.8 combat: sprint/KB-enchant extra knockback uses 1.8.9 addVelocity semantics
+            // 1.8.9 (EntityPlayer.attackTargetEntityWithCurrentItem) applied the extra as
+            //   target.addVelocity(-sin(yaw) * i * 0.5, 0.1, cos(yaw) * i * 0.5)
+            // a pure ADD on top of the base-knockback motion, with a flat +0.1 vertical.
+            // modern folds it through LivingEntity.knockback(), which HALVES the target's
+            // already-knocked-back motion again and re-applies the capped vertical kick:
+            // a ground sprint-hit lands at ~0.7 horizontal / 0.4 vertical instead of the
+            // authentic 0.9 / 0.46. push() has exact addVelocity semantics (plus the Paper
+            // EntityPushedByEntityAttackEvent for plugin compat) and sets needsSync for
+            // spectators; hurtMarked makes the victim's own client receive the motion
+            // packet via the block below. knockback-scale still applies so the operator
+            // tuning knob covers the extra hit like it covers the base hit.
+            double rapierKbScale = net.minecraft.server.rapier.RapierConfig.knockbackScale();
+            target.push(
+                -Mth.sin(this.getYRot() * (float) (Math.PI / 180.0)) * strength * rapierKbScale, 0.1 * rapierKbScale, Mth.cos(this.getYRot() * (float) (Math.PI / 180.0)) * strength * rapierKbScale
+                , this // Paper - Add EntityKnockbackByEntityEvent and EntityPushedByEntityAttackEvent
+            );
+            target.hurtMarked = true;
+            // rapier end
 
             // rapier - configurable attacker momentum damping (was hardcoded 0.6 = authentic 1.8.9)
             double rapierAttackMomentumScale = net.minecraft.server.rapier.RapierConfig.attackMomentumScale();
